What are Grinding Wheels for Wafers?
Grinding wheels for wafers are precision-engineered tools designed to thin and shape silicon wafers with micrometer-level accuracy. These specialized abrasives typically incorporate diamond or cubic boron nitride (CBN) particles bonded to substrates using vitrified or resinoid matrices. The tools play a critical role in semiconductor back-grinding processes, enabling the production of thinner wafers while maintaining structural integrity and minimizing subsurface damage.
